{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "p11u.rgb-session.command-jobs.001",
  "date": "2026-10-22",
  "state": "scoped-qualified",
  "acceptance": false,
  "complete_requirement_coverage": false,
  "scope": "New immutable C++/Python session commands retain complete ordered plane visits, frozen selections, promoted/current stages and final stack policy in an independent closed V1 profile. A singleton existing RGB capture carries source ownership/current navigation, while the session plan defines its own processing membership. Borrowed capture/job admission precedes encoding and worker reads. Descriptor-only historical geometry validation is shared by session admission and record validation, including float/integer processor bounds; malformed late geometry is rejected without allocating masks or acquiring source samples. Strict replay checks original identity/revisions, storage/calibration, selection, active source position and display. Explicit source rebinding validates the complete original first and preserves all saved absolute positions, selections and policies, then checks destination compatibility; destination navigation and live selection survive. It does not silently adopt current selection or translate historical anchors. Common ContrastApplyJob submission uses admitted reservations, worker-only source processing, cooperative blocked-reader cancellation, queued-source release, immutable retained records, escaped snapshot/Dataset/C++ plane leases and one original-owner/all-revision guarded paired publication. Native cases prove callback freezing, blocked reads/cancel, no creator-thread IO, complete records, paired Undo and plane-alias reservation retention after publication/close/shutdown. Installed C++ SDK consumers cover literal multi-visit component composition, final noncurrent narrowed stack mapping, captured worker publication, strict decode, Undo and explicit destination replay. All 378 ImageJ navigation rows exercise both returning Reset/remap complete hashes through captured commands, JSON strict replay, worker preview/publication, Undo/Redo and explicit new-source replay. All 5292 ImageJ single-visit stack rows pass complete captured worker output hashes. Closed grammar/late corruption, all source domains, admission refusal before IO, detached Python values, public exports, escaped leases and explicit historical-membership retention also pass. Windows/Linux each pass 22 native suites, three existing standalone full C++ UI probes, two installed SDK consumers, ten background repetitions, four hidden GL contexts and 45319 installed Python cases (5715 new), zero failure/error/skip. Actual disposable installed venv interpreters are used; Linux full tests use the SHA-verified 5481-file final native snapshot. Two preliminary Python fixture mistakes (method call vs property, then a C++-only mask constructor) are retained as failed evidence; corrected full suites run final tests, including a stronger original-position guard against a larger destination. Final test-only amendment changes no production/native test input after native qualification; both manifests and raw variants are pinned. Existing scalar, uniform RGB and stack V1 wires, processing arithmetic and main-panel behavior remain unchanged. Full session portable workflow/Batch/review and shared ImGui transitions remain open, as do combined upstream promotion/navigation/final-stack traces and full G057/ImageJ/Fiji/platform/resource acceptance. Estimates cover declared owned work; source/provider caches, caller/frontend copies, publication/history staging and RSS remain external. Exact prototype/final scratch is CRC/every-member-SHA archived before confined deletion; final installs/probes/logs and useful caches remain. All original 99 requirement/status triples are unchanged and the old Auto producer-source evidence gate is not repinned or relaxed.",
